
<p>Abby Haddican:</p>

<blockquote>
  <p>Times New Resistance autocorrects specific words as they are
typed. For example, the word <em>ICE</em> autocorrects to <em>the Goon
Squad</em> and the word <em>Trump</em> autocorrects to <em>Donald Trump is
a felon</em>.</p>

<p>To the untrained eye, Times New Resistance looks just like Times
New Roman — <a href="https://www.npr.org/2025/12/11/nx-s1-5639915/u-s-state-department-changes-official-font-from-calibri-back-to-times-new-roman">the official font of the U.S. State
Department</a>. When you install the font, <em>it will appear in
your font menus as Times &nbsp;New Roman</em>, with an extra space
between the words Times and New.</p>
</blockquote>

<p>Ligatures, man. Will they never cease <a href="https://daringfireball.net/linked/2020/05/13/scunthorpe-sans">to surprise</a>?</p>

